{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review exact head 94f2d8f592a83882483a874cc75b75ecb385d7d6, branch request/needs-action-ratification, reported by artifact 0a153f09 at path ui.\n\nThis is self-initiated work, authorized by hugh on 2026-08-22 to carry forward the substance of request 4c739023 without a self-request. The motivating decision is the supersession act 654cb674 that retired that request and recorded its substance; the implementing commit rests on it. There is no promise and no separate report - the artifact is the report.\n\nThe change: the work list iterates projection.commitments, so ratification obligations, which are not commitments, could never reach the screen. They are now a third population beside the two summary lines already there, each reached from its own count.\n\nPlease be hardest on these three, which are where I could most easily be wrong.\n\nFirst, the discriminator. I count a kind when its vocabulary definition has satisfier role:ratifier and render is not note. That excludes assert deliberately - 403 of them - on the reasoning that an assert stands on its author's signature and is not inert without ratification. If that reasoning is wrong the queue is silently under-reporting, which is the same defect as the one being fixed. It also admits admission-profile, infra-key, kind-def and seal, which I have not seen in the wild; check I have not admitted something that is never actually owed.\n\nSecond, the unresolvable case. With no ratifier or with several the row names nobody and the screen says which case it is. Check that an empty queue and an undischargeable queue cannot be confused on screen, because reading empty as nothing-owed is exactly the failure the original request identified one level down.\n\nThird, whether this is worth its size at all. Simplification is a required conclusion and I would rather be told to cut it than defend it. In particular, RowState gained a sixth member for a population that never mixes with the other five, and I am not sure that earns its place.\n\nTwo of the retired request's conditions no longer describe the code: WorkDrawer.tsx, workItemNeedsAction and needsCount are gone, taking the me-resolution and topic-summing defects with them. I have said so in the artifact rather than claiming to have fixed them. If you think the conditions still bind in some other form, say so - that is a changes-requested I would accept.\n\nGates at the exact head: npx tsc --noEmit clean, npm test 68 pass 0 fail. No Go file changed, so the Go gates were not run; make docs passes on main at 7a02f3e1 independently of this branch. Five mutations of the seam were each caught by the new tests; the mutation list is in the artifact.\n\nOne thing that is not yours to decide but that you should see. Path ui already carries two live artifacts, 3d89c5e0 (mine, in main) and a944f670 (planner's, commit 39fc1720, not in main, no review request). Mine is now a third. Whoever merges first must retire the others and I cannot retire planner's, so the ordering needs settling before any merge. Do not let that block the verdict - it is a merge-time problem, not a defect in this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0a153f09effdb3f6f051c15f52c0f914a7a6e242","conditions":"the queue is derived from the vocabulary rather than a hardcoded kind list; the ratification population is kept separate from the commitment population and never summed into one figure; an item belonging to no commitment and no thread still appears; an unresolvable ratifier is stated on screen rather than rendering as nothing owed; npx tsc --noEmit is clean and npm test is green at the exact head; architecture, security and simplification conclusions are recorded","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}